From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Thomas Lamprecht <t.lamprecht@proxmox.com>
Date: Tue, 10 Nov 2026 15:05:46 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] PVE backup: vma reader: fix verbose restore of disks below 64
 KiB

The progress output divides by the number of clusters in the archive,
which was rounded down per device. If all devices are smaller than one
64 KiB cluster, that is zero and vma died with SIGFPE on restore and
verify. qemu-server always restores with verbose output.

Round the count up per device, and skip the progress output if there
is nothing to count, as for a restore of only a vmstate stream.

Signed-off-by: Thomas Lamprecht <t.lamprecht@proxmox.com>
Acked-by: Wolfgang Bumiller <w.bumiller@proxmox.com>
---
 vma-reader.c | 5 +++--
 1 file changed, 3 insertions(+), 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/vma-reader.c b/vma-reader.c
index 8350fe89cb..1d80eed043 100644
--- a/vma-reader.c
+++ b/vma-reader.c
@@ -461,7 +461,7 @@ static void allocate_rstate(VmaReader *vmar,  guint8 dev_id,
     vmar->rstate[dev_id].bitmap_size = bitmap_size;
     vmar->rstate[dev_id].bitmap = g_new0(unsigned long, bitmap_size);
 
-    vmar->cluster_count += size/VMA_CLUSTER_SIZE;
+    vmar->cluster_count += DIV_ROUND_UP(size, VMA_CLUSTER_SIZE);
 }
 
 int vma_reader_register_bs(VmaReader *vmar, guint8 dev_id, BlockBackend *target,
@@ -673,7 +673,8 @@ static int restore_extent(VmaReader *vmar, unsigned char *buf,
 
         vmar->clusters_read++;
 
-        if (verbose) {
+        /* on restore, the count leaves out a vmstate stream, which can be all */
+        if (verbose && vmar->cluster_count) {
             time_t duration = time(NULL) - vmar->start_time;
             int percent = (vmar->clusters_read*100)/vmar->cluster_count;
             if (percent != vmar->clusters_read_per) {
